<title>USA: LESLIE-ADM SOYBEAN PRODUCTION SURVEY BY STATE.</title>
<headline>LESLIE-ADM SOYBEAN PRODUCTION SURVEY BY STATE.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following tables contain state-by-state soybean production estimates published in the Leslie-ADM Investor Services Crop survey.</p>
<p>U.S. SOYBEAN PRODUCTION (IN 000'S BUSHELS)</p>
<p>	  LESLIE  8/1/97   USDA 1996   USDA 1995</p>
<p> PENN	   13,505	11,400	 9,450</p>
<p> OHIO	  181,845     157,150     153,140</p>
<p> INDIANA     235,335     203,680     196,710</p>
<p> ILLINOIS    412,925     398,925     378,300</p>
<p> MICHIGAN     70,875	46,740	59,600</p>
<p> WISCONSIN    43,680	32,190	34,400</p>
<p>U.S. SOYBEAN PRODUCTION</p>
<p>	  LESLIE  8/1/97   USDA 1996   USDA 1995</p>
<p> MINN	  291,450     224,200     234,900</p>
<p> IOWA	  499,200     415,800     407,440</p>
<p> MISSOURI    152,775     149,850     132,750</p>
<p> N DAKOTA     35,475	24,505	18,560</p>
<p> S DAKOTA    127,650	90,780	75,000</p>
<p> NEBRASKA    141,450     135,450     100,980</p>
<p> KANSAS	 80,500	74,000	51,250</p>
